@page "/data-deletion"
@{
  ViewData["Title"] = "Data Deletion — Queenzone";
  ViewData["Description"] = "How to request deletion of your personal data from Queenzone.";
  ViewData["CanonicalPath"] = "/data-deletion";
}

<partial name="_PageHero" model='@(("Your Data", "Data Deletion", "How to remove your personal information from Queenzone.", "Last updated 9 October 2026"))' />

<section class="qz-section qz-section--warm">
  <div class="qz-container qz-container--text">

    <p class="lede">You can delete your account and personal sign-in data at any time.</p>

    <h2>What we store</h2>
    <p>If you have a Queenzone account, we store your email address, display name, and (where applicable) a reference to the social login provider you used (Google, Microsoft, Discord, GitHub, or Apple). We do not store passwords in plain text.</p>

    <h2>How to delete your account</h2>
    <p>In the app, open Settings → Delete my account. On the website, sign in, open <a href="/account/settings">Account settings</a>, and select <strong>Delete my account</strong>. Type DELETE to confirm. Your account will be disabled and you will be signed out.</p>
    <p>If you cannot sign in, use the <a href="/contact">Contact</a> form or email <a href="mailto:support@queenzone.org">support@queenzone.org</a> from the address associated with your account.</p>

    <h2>What happens after the request</h2>
    <p>Your profile and avatar are hidden immediately. We remove your email address, password hash, social sign-in references, modern posts and messages, submitted content, and uploads. Posts and messages become deleted placeholders where other members' conversations or threads need to remain coherent. Uploaded files and Sign in with Apple tokens may finish removing through a retrying background process. Your legacy public archive posts remain, but their link to your modern account is removed.</p>
    <p>We provide a private status receipt after confirmation. It works after sign-out and shows when removal is complete; save its page address if cleanup is still in progress. Immediate deletion cannot be cancelled. If you previously scheduled deletion under the older 30-day policy, you may still sign in and cancel that request before its due date. If you use Sign in with Apple, you can also remove QueenZone under Apple Account Settings → Sign in with Apple.</p>

    <h2>Diagnostics held by service providers</h2>
    <p>Deleting your account does not automatically erase Sentry diagnostics, operational logs or backups. The private account-deletion receipt covers our account and upload cleanup, not a provider-wide deletion.</p>
    <p>Account-deletion requests also need a manual review of identifiable diagnostics associated with your account. For requests or follow-up, use the <a href="/contact">Contact</a> form or email <a href="mailto:support@queenzone.org">support@queenzone.org</a>. Tell us that you have requested account deletion and, if useful, the approximate date of the app problem and your app version. Do not send passwords, access tokens or private message content. We may ask for the minimum information needed to verify your request.</p>
    <p>We will explain which data we can associate with you and remove or ask the provider to remove, and any remaining retention limits. Some diagnostic events cannot be linked to an account; older events and backups may remain until their retention period expires. This is a manual review of account-associated data, not an automated provider purge or a separate service for selectively deleting account content. See our <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a> for provider information.</p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>For any questions about your data, use the <a href="/contact">Contact</a> form or email <a href="mailto:support@queenzone.org">support@queenzone.org</a>.</p>

  </div>
</section>
